IMPORT prelude

-- Maintenance of Parents Act 1995 (Singapore) -- who may claim maintenance from a child (s 3(1), (3), (5), (6)), the child under 21
-- (s 3AA), the parent's record of abandonment, abuse or neglect (ss 3B, 12A), when the Tribunal may order maintenance and the
-- abandonment defence (s 5(1), (4), (5), (7)), how long an order lasts (s 7), who may apply for a parent who cannot (s 11), who may
-- represent a party (ss 12C, 14(3), (4)), contempt (s 15), and the routes out of the Tribunal (ss 3(8), 8(6), 17, 18(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 5/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MPA1995.txt. The cover says the revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the
-- latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 19 of 2025 (wef 05/12/2025). Most of the provisions below were rewritten by Act 22 of
-- 2023 (wef 01/07/2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the Act under which an elderly parent in Singapore can make an adult
-- child pay for his or her upkeep. SCOPED to the claim itself. Not encoded: the Commissioner's other conciliation powers (s 12(5)-(8)),
-- conciliation for destitute persons (s 12B), the security, deposit and direction powers (s 6), variation grounds (s 8(1)-(3)),
-- enforcement through the Women's Charter (s 10), the constitution of the Tribunal (s 13), information-gathering and its
-- confidentiality (s 14A), special cases (s 16), privacy of hearings (s 19), costs (s 20), and the factors of s 5(2) (they shape the
-- amount, which the Act leaves to the Tribunal). The content of a "record or purported record of abandonment, abuse or neglect" is
-- "prescribed" (s 2) and the prescribing regulations were not retrieved; here it is a yes/no fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Maintenance of Parents Act 1995 -- maintenance`

§§ `3(1), (5), (6) -- who may claim`

-- s 3(1): "any person domiciled and resident in Singapore who is of or above 60 years of age and who is unable to maintain himself or
-- herself adequately" may apply for an order that "one or more of the person's children" pay a monthly allowance, other periodical
-- payment or lump sum. s 2: "child" includes "an illegitimate child, an adopted child or a stepchild".
-- s 3(5): unable to maintain if "total or expected income and other financial resources are inadequate to provide the parent with
-- basic amenities and basic physical needs including (but not limited to) shelter, food, medical costs and clothing".
-- s 3(6): below 60, the Act still applies if the Tribunal is satisfied of "infirmity of mind or body" preventing or making it
-- difficult to maintain oneself, "or that there is any other special reason".
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `domiciled in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `resources adequate for basic needs` IS A BOOLEAN, `infirmity or other special reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent may claim maintenance` IF
        `domiciled in Singapore`
    AND `resident in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `resources adequate for basic needs`)
    AND (`age` AT LEAST 60 OR `infirmity or other special reason`)

§§ `3AA -- the child below 21`

-- s 3AA(1): "A child who is below 21 years of age is not liable to maintain the child's parent." (2): a claim "must not be referred to
-- the Commissioner" against the child and the child "must not be named or joined as a respondent". Added by Act 19 of 2025.
GIVEN `child's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child can be named as a respondent` IF
    `child's age` AT LEAST 21

§§ `3(3) -- the Commissioner first`

-- s 3(3): any person "(except the Commissioner)" applying "in respect of any claim for which no application had previously been made
-- under this section must, before making the application, refer the claim to the Commissioner".
-- s 12(6): if the claim "has not been settled" after referral or conciliation, an application may then be made to the Tribunal.
GIVEN `applicant is the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `an application was previously made on the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim must first be referred to the Commissioner` IF
    (NOT `applicant is the Commissioner`) AND (NOT `an application was previously made on the claim`)

§§ `3B and 12A -- the parent's record of abandonment, abuse or neglect`

-- s 3B(1): permission must first be obtained if (a) the s 3A declaration "states that the parent has a record or purported record of
-- abandonment, abuse or neglect of the child"; (b) the Commissioner notifies (or ascertains) that the parent has such a record; or
-- (c) a conciliation officer discontinues conciliation under s 12A(2).
GIVEN `declaration states a record` IS A BOOLEAN, `Commissioner finds a record` IS A BOOLEAN, `conciliation discontinued for a record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permission is needed to apply` IF
    `declaration states a record` OR `Commissioner finds a record` OR `conciliation discontinued for a record`

-- s 3B(7): permission may be granted "if there is a good arguable case that (a) the parent did not abandon, abuse or neglect the child;
-- or (b) the child should maintain the parent on just and equitable grounds".
GIVEN `good arguable case of no abandonment` IS A BOOLEAN, `good arguable case on just and equitable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permission may be granted` IF
    `good arguable case of no abandonment` OR `good arguable case on just and equitable grounds`

-- s 3B(2): the permission application is dealt with "without informing or involving the child, except where (a) the child was
-- involved in any conciliation ... that is discontinued under section 12A(2); and (b) the child informs the conciliation officer or
-- the Commissioner that the child wishes, or is willing, to participate".
GIVEN `child was in the discontinued conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN, `child wishes to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is involved in the permission application` IF
    `child was in the discontinued conciliation` AND `child wishes to participate`

-- s 12A(1): the Commissioner "must not refer any matter ... for conciliation" if the declaration states, or the Commissioner
-- ascertains, a record of abandonment, abuse or neglect of the child, "unless permission is granted under section 3B".
GIVEN `a record is declared or ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 3B permission granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may refer the matter for conciliation` IF
    (NOT `a record is declared or ascertained`) OR `section 3B permission granted`

§§ `5(1), (4), (5), (7) -- the maintenance order`

-- s 5(1): the Tribunal may make an order "if it considers that it is just and equitable that the respondent should maintain the parent
-- and that (a) the respondent is able to provide maintenance to the parent after the respondent's own requirements and those of his or
-- her spouse and his or her children have been supplied; and (b) the parent is unable, in spite of efforts on his or her part, to
-- maintain himself or herself through work or from his or her property or from any other source". Read with s 3AA(1).
GIVEN `just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN, `respondent able after own family's needs` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `parent unable despite efforts` IS A BOOLEAN, `respondent's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may order maintenance` IF
        `just and equitable`
    AND `respondent able after own family's needs`
    AND `parent unable despite efforts`
    AND `the child can be named as a respondent` `respondent's age`

-- s 5(4): "If the Tribunal is satisfied upon due proof that the parent abandoned, abused or neglected the respondent, it may dismiss
-- the application or may reduce the quantum". (5): "The onus of proving abandonment, abuse or neglect is on the respondent alleging it."
-- An allegation not proved by the respondent opens neither course.
GIVEN `respondent alleges abandonment` IS A BOOLEAN, `respondent proves abandonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may dismiss or reduce for abandonment` IF
    `respondent alleges abandonment` AND `respondent proves abandonment`

-- s 5(7): before hearing an application under s 5 the Tribunal "must ... refer the differences between the parties to a mediator".
-- s 8(4): on an application to vary or rescind, it "may" do so "where it considers it necessary or desirable".
GIVEN `is a variation application` IS A BOOLEAN, `Tribunal considers mediation necessary or desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `mediation is required before the hearing` IF
    (NOT `is a variation application`) OR `Tribunal considers mediation necessary or desirable`

§§ `7 -- how long an order lasts`

-- s 7(1): unless expressed for a shorter period or rescinded, an order expires "(a) if the maintenance was unsecured -- on the death of
-- the parent or the respondent, whichever is the earlier; or (b) if the maintenance was secured -- on the death of the parent".
GIVEN `secured` IS A BOOLEAN, `parent has died` IS A BOOLEAN, `respondent has died` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `shorter period has run out` IS A BOOLEAN, `rescinded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has ended` IF
        `rescinded`
    OR  `shorter period has run out`
    OR  `parent has died`
    OR  ((NOT `secured`) AND `respondent has died`)

§§ `11 -- applying for a parent who cannot`

-- s 11(1): where a parent is unable to apply "(whether by reason of physical or mental infirmity or for any other reason)" the
-- application may be made by "(a) any family member of the parent; (b) any person in whose care the parent resides; or (c) any other
-- person whom the parent has authorised". (2): the Director-General of Social Welfare or a protector, if the parent is a vulnerable
-- adult under a court order under s 14 or 15 of the Vulnerable Adults Act 2018 or a Part 2 power has been exercised.
-- s 12(2): the Commissioner may apply for a parent of or above 60 "whether or not the parent is able to do so" (s 12(4): below 60 on
-- infirmity or special reason) -- not encoded here.
DECLARE Proxy IS ONE OF
    `a family member`
    `the person the parent lives with in care`
    `a person the parent authorised`
    `a neighbour not authorised`
    `the Director-General of Social Welfare`

GIVEN `the proxy` IS A Proxy, `parent is unable to apply` IS A BOOLEAN, `parent is a vulnerable adult under the 2018 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proxy may apply for the parent` IF
    `parent is unable to apply` AND
        (CONSIDER `the proxy`
         WHEN `a family member` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the person the parent lives with in care` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a person the parent authorised` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Director-General of Social Welfare` THEN `parent is a vulnerable adult under the 2018 Act`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `12C, 14(3), (4) -- who may speak for a party`

-- s 14(4): "No party to any proceedings before the Tribunal may be represented by an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court except
-- that the Commissioner may represent the applicant". s 12C(2), (3): the same for conciliation and mediation.
-- s 14(3): a party may be represented (a) "by an agent acting without fee, gain, reward or any expectation thereof" where the Tribunal
-- "at the party's request and for good reason" permits; (b) if the party is the parent as applicant, by the Commissioner; (c) if the
-- party is an approved person or organisation, by its employee or officer.
DECLARE Representative IS ONE OF
    `a lawyer the party engages`
    `the Commissioner`
    `an unpaid agent`
    `a paid agent`
    `an employee of the approved organisation`

GIVEN `the representative` IS A Representative, `party is the parent as applicant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `party is an approved organisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `Tribunal permits the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representative may appear before the Tribunal` IF
    CONSIDER `the representative`
    WHEN `the Commissioner` THEN `party is the parent as applicant`
    WHEN `an unpaid agent` THEN `Tribunal permits the agent`
    WHEN `an employee of the approved organisation` THEN `party is an approved organisation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `15 -- contempt of the Tribunal`

-- s 15(1): assaulting, wilfully insulting or obstructing Tribunal members, officers or witnesses, misbehaving at a sitting, or disobeying
-- an order "without lawful excuse" during a sitting -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 6 months". The text says "or", not "or both".
`the maximum contempt fine in dollars` MEANS 5000
`the maximum contempt imprisonment in months` MEANS 6

§§ `3(8), 8(6), 17, 18(2) -- the routes out of the Tribunal`

-- s 3(8): an applicant aggrieved by a dismissal under s 3(7) (frivolous or vexatious, or failure to comply with s 3(3), 3A or 3B) may
-- "within 14 days of the decision, appeal in writing to the Tribunal". s 8(6): the same, "within 14 days after", for a dismissed
-- variation application. s 17(1): a party aggrieved on a point of law may apply to the High Court "within 14 days". The day of the
-- decision is taken here as day 0; the text does not say how the 14 days are counted (inference).
GIVEN `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 14-day challenge is in time` IF
    `days since the decision` AT MOST 14

-- s 18(2): an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court "upon any question of law or of mixed law and fact except in any
-- case where the Tribunal has made the order with the consent of the parties", including a s 5(3) consent order, "unless it is alleged
-- that the consent was obtained by means of fraud, duress, threat or misrepresentation".
DECLARE Question IS ONE OF
    `a question of law`
    `a question of mixed law and fact`
    `a question of fact only`

GIVEN `the question` IS A Question, `order made by consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent alleged obtained by fraud, duress, threat or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies to the High Court` IF
        (CONSIDER `the question`
         WHEN `a question of fact only` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND ((NOT `order made by consent`) OR `consent alleged obtained by fraud, duress, threat or misrepresentation`)

-- s 17(2): the High Court's powers of revision "do not extend to a decision of the Tribunal as to the quantum of maintenance awarded
-- or apportioned".
GIVEN `the decision is about the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court may revise the decision` IF
    NOT `the decision is about the amount`
